From: BT2 DS216 portability qualification
Subject: [PATCH] runtimeconfig: make compile-time guards word-size neutral

Base: openai/tunnel-client@a390c168ff1b2d14e73a95991c186c6aba3ff5a0

The six assertions below exist only to make negative constant relationships fail
at compile time. Using uint accidentally also requires every positive duration
constant to fit the target machine word. Preserve the nonnegative assertion
while making it independent of 32-bit vs 64-bit target word size.

--- a/pkg/runtimeconfig/config.go
+++ b/pkg/runtimeconfig/config.go
@@ -77,12 +77,12 @@ const (
 const DefaultControlPlaneBaseURL = defaultControlPlaneBaseURL
 
-const _ = uint(maxControlPlaneMaxInFlight - defaultControlPlaneMaxInFlight)
-const _ = uint(defaultControlPlanePollTimeout - 1)
-const _ = uint(defaultControlPlaneInitialPollTimeout - 1)
-const _ = uint(maxControlPlanePollDeadline - defaultControlPlanePollTimeout - defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail)
-const _ = uint(defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - 1)
-const _ = uint(maxControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - 1)
+const _ = uint64(maxControlPlaneMaxInFlight - defaultControlPlaneMaxInFlight)
+const _ = uint64(defaultControlPlanePollTimeout - 1)
+const _ = uint64(defaultControlPlaneInitialPollTimeout - 1)
+const _ = uint64(maxControlPlanePollDeadline - defaultControlPlanePollTimeout - defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail)
+const _ = uint64(defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - 1)
+const _ = uint64(maxControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - defaultControlPlanePollDeadlineGuardrail - 1)
 
 var harpoonLabelPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`)
